Since $A(4,21)$ is on $y=g(x)$, we have $g(4)=21$.
$$\begin{aligned}21&=-2f(4\cdot 4+4)+1\\21&=-2f(20)+1\\20&=-2f(20)\\f(20)&=-10\end{aligned}$$
$$\therefore\ \text{the point on } y=f(x) \text{ is } (20,-10)$$
Alternatively, $g(x)=-2f(4x+4)+1$ is obtained from $y=f(x)$ by a horizontal dilation of factor $\dfrac{1}{4}$, a translation left 1, a vertical dilation of factor $-2$ and a translation up 1.

Reverse these steps on $(4,21)$:

down 1 gives $(4,20)$;

vertical dilation of factor $-\dfrac{1}{2}$ gives $(4,-10)$;

right 1 gives $(5,-10)$;

horizontal dilation of factor $4$ gives $(20,-10)$.

